Follow the instructions below and prepare a Prompt (MD file) to:
create the working design of a trading app in python for Indian stock market that runs on angelone api.

Expected functionality of this app:
1) It should be able to login using saved api credentials in an .env file when market opens for the day.
2) It should be able to keep scanning the live market during market hours.
3) It should be able to read:
	- real time tick data of index futures along with volume.
	- real time open interest data of the same index option chain.
	Note: Name of the index should be provided by the user in config.yaml
4) It should be able to find the trend (positive or negative) of the index using: 
	- index futures volume breakout and 
	- options' open interest, PCR, Change in OI etc.
5) Once a trend is recognized with strong indicator, It should be able to place an order within real time:
	- buy at the money CE option for positive trend, or
	- buy at the money PE option for negative trend
6) Once a trade is open, the app should keep scanning for the trend and exit the trade in timely manner so that there is maximum gain and minimum loss.
7) the app should be able to update the date wise profit/loss in an excel file for evaluating the efficiency of the app in long run.
6) the app should be able to do paper trade to test this functionality before actually implementing it with real money.
7) the app should be able to keep running during the market time, but don't open any trade after 2:30 pm.
8) Once a trade is open for the day, it should not open any more trades on that day. Strictly no more than one trade per day.
9) keep all the user variables in a yaml file that can be changed as per the needs of the user. Some such variables are:
	- index name (BANKNIFTY)
	- candle duration (1,5,15)
	- Max loss per day (1000, 2000, 5000)
	- trailing stoploss (True or False)
	- one trade per day (True or False)
	- Re entry allowed (True or False)
	- No new trade after this time ("14:30")
	- number of lots to trade (1,2,5,10)
	- mode (whether paper or real trade) etc.
	- notifications enabled (True or False)
	- keep retrying after network timeout (True or False)
If anything is missing here, feel free to suggest and add to the prompt.